    "build": "Playtest feedback, round 23",
    "text": "Super cups: one match at a neutral ground early in each season, 122 of them. In every nation the league champions meet the cup winners (the league's runner-up when one club did both); on each continent the champions cup winner meets the winner of its Shield (the European, South American, African, Asian and North American Super Cups). They have their own day after the first league round, a card on the Cups screen, count as a trophy for the winner and are kept apart from the season's cups in the archive. A new world has none in its first season (there is no last season). Six more regional club cups, groups of four then a final like the other regional cups: the Arab Club Cup (eight Arab leagues, taking the places after the Gulf Club Cup's), the West African Club Cup, the East and Southern African Club Cup, the Central American Club Cup, the Andean Club Cup and the Atlantic Club Cup (Scotland, Wales, Ireland and Northern Ireland). 22 continental cups in all, none of them with a club in two of them. Fifteen more regional tournaments for nations: the East African, Southern African, West African, North African, Arab, Central Asian, Nordic, Central European, Celtic, Caucasus, Central American and Caribbean, Andean and River Plate cups, the Baltic Cup and the Balkan Cup join the Southeast Asian, Gulf and East Asian ones and the three older invitationals: a host that rotates through the region's nations and the three best-ranked others. Three are played each season in turn (no nation in two of them, and none in a season where the host or guests have qualifiers in the window), so each comes round about every seven seasons.",
